Table full name: NEW_YORK.NEW_YORK.TREE_CENSUS_2015
Column name: boro_ct Type: NUMBER Description: This is the boro_ct identifyer for the census tract that the tree point falls into.
Column name: health Type: TEXT Description: Indicates the user's perception of tree health.
Column name: st_assem Type: NUMBER Description: State Assembly District in which tree point is located
Column name: boroname Type: TEXT Description: Name of borough in which tree point is located
Column name: root_other Type: TEXT Description: Indicates the presence of other root problems
Column name: problems Type: TEXT
Column name: st_senate Type: NUMBER Description: State Senate District in which tree point is located
Column name: y_sp Type: FLOAT Description: Y coordinate, in state plane. Units are feet
Column name: borocode Type: NUMBER Description: Code for borough in which tree point is located
Column name: longitude Type: FLOAT Description: Longitude of point, in decimal degrees
Column name: trunk_wire Type: TEXT Description: Indicates the presence of a trunk problem caused by wires or rope wrapped around the trunk
Column name: nta_name Type: TEXT Description: This is the NTA name corresponding to the neighborhood tabulation area from the 2010 US Census that the tree point falls into.
Column name: tree_id Type: NUMBER Description: Unique identification number for each tree point
Column name: stump_diam Type: NUMBER Description: Diameter of stump measured through the center, rounded to the nearest inch.
Column name: x_sp Type: FLOAT Description: X coordinate, in state plane. Units are feet.
Column name: block_id Type: NUMBER Description: Identifier linking each tree to the block in the blockface table/shapefile that it is mapped on.
Column name: zip_city Type: TEXT Description: City as derived from zipcode. This is often (but not always) the same as borough.
Column name: brch_other Type: TEXT Description: Indicates the presence of other branch problems
Column name: state Type: TEXT Description: All features given value 'New York'
Column name: cb_num Type: NUMBER Description: Community board in which tree point is located
Column name: cncldist Type: NUMBER Description: Council district in which tree point is located
Column name: user_type Type: TEXT Description: This field describes the category of user who collected this tree point's data.
Column name: trnk_light Type: TEXT Description: Indicates the presence of a trunk problem caused by lighting installed on the tree
Column name: address Type: TEXT Description: Nearest estimated address to tree
Column name: zipcode Type: NUMBER Description: Five-digit zipcode in which tree is located
Column name: root_grate Type: TEXT Description: Indicates the presence of a root problem caused by metal grates in tree bed
Column name: spc_common Type: TEXT Description: Common name for species, e.g. "red maple"
Column name: nta Type: TEXT Description: This is the NTA Code corresponding to the neighborhood tabulation area from the 2010 US Census that the tree point falls into.
Column name: brch_shoe Type: TEXT Description: Indicates the presence of a branch problem caused by sneakers in the branches
Column name: spc_latin Type: TEXT Description: Scientific name for species, e.g. "Acer rubrum"
Column name: status Type: TEXT Description: Indicates whether the tree is alive, standing dead, or a stump.
Column name: guards Type: TEXT Description: Indicates whether a guard is present, and if the user felt it was a helpful or harmful guard. Not recorded for dead trees and stumps
Column name: steward Type: TEXT Description: Indicates the number of unique signs of stewardship observed for this tree. Not recorded for stumps or dead trees.
Column name: sidewalk Type: TEXT Description: Indicates whether one of the sidewalk flags immediately adjacent to the tree was damaged, cracked, or lifted. Not recorded for dead trees and stumps.
Column name: root_stone Type: TEXT Description: Indicates the presence of a root problem caused by paving stones in tree bed
Column name: created_at Type: DATE Description: The date tree points were collected in the census software
Column name: curb_loc Type: TEXT Description: Location of tree bed in relationship to the curb; trees are either along the curb (OnCurb) or offset from the curb (OffsetFromCurb)
Column name: latitude Type: FLOAT Description: Latitude of point, in decimal degrees
Column name: trnk_other Type: TEXT Description: Indicates the presence of other trunk problems
Column name: tree_dbh Type: NUMBER Description: Diameter of the tree, measured at approximately 54" / 137cm above the ground.
Column name: brch_light Type: TEXT Description: Indicates the presence of a branch problem caused by lights (usually string lights) or wires in the branches
